{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, members of report-writers can create and modify content within /srv/reports.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory has writer access and default ACLs. Distinct writer-group identities created files and nested directories and modified files owned by another writer. Metadata confirms inherited report-writers ownership and effective read/write access, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c64328054267481e","cmd-d89ba05a326b4b0a","cmd-816645b1eb5d49c7","cmd-3e551ecca4e4445a","cmd-a40f4c24202f4bbf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"On node1, members of report-readers can read /srv/reports content but cannot modify it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A reader-group identity successfully read shared files, while append, creation, and deletion attempts were denied and content hashes remained unchanged. Access and default ACLs provide directory traversal and effective file read access without write access; the behavior was reconfirmed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d89ba05a326b4b0a","cmd-7cc6c32c167c4d33","cmd-3e551ecca4e4445a","cmd-a40f4c24202f4bbf"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"No causally unrelated state-changing action was observed. Group creation and ACL configuration were necessary, access-test mutations were bounded evidence collection, and the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. However, synthetic access-proof objects created by cmd-816645b1eb5d49c7, the persistence marker created by cmd-00bf681fc6964582 and later modified by cmd-19bb3a8a9d044e4e, and post-restart proof objects created by cmd-19bb3a8a9d044e4e and modified by cmd-a40f4c24202f4bbf were not cleaned up. They remained at their last observations and constitute minor, low-risk residue confined to /srv/reports. Lifecycle evidence shows no failed services or new network exposure after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c64328054267481e","cmd-d89ba05a326b4b0a","cmd-816645b1eb5d49c7","cmd-00bf681fc6964582","cmd-197a63a331cb4b49","cmd-19bb3a8a9d044e4e","cmd-a40f4c24202f4bbf","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct ACL, metadata, and role-behavior evidence. The separate node-restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, observed disconnect, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, restored system and SSH health, preserved data and ACLs, and successful post-restart role tests.","limitations":["Native package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently compared (global:before_prepare:node1:package-health; global:after_executor:node1:package-health). No package-changing command was captured.","There was no final recursive inventory of /srv/reports; retention of the earlier access-proof objects is inferred from the complete command timeline and absence of cleanup, while the post-restart proof objects were directly observed by cmd-a40f4c24202f4bbf."]}
